---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import links from "../data/links.json";
---
<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section class="section wrap">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      I'm a software engineer learning how modern large language models are
      built — from Transformer fundamentals to reasoning, Mixture-of-Experts,
      inference, and eventually original research. This site (and its
      <a href={links.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">source repo</a>)
      is a public, working lab notebook for that journey.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am <strong>not</strong> claiming to be an AI expert. I am documenting
      the process of becoming one — in the open, with real code, real
      failures, and real results.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>Labels, used precisely</h2>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Learning</strong></td><td>Understanding an existing, published concept.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Implementation</strong></td><td>Building an existing, published idea from scratch.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Reproduction</strong></td><td>Attempting to reproduce published findings (usually small-scale).</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Experiment</strong></td><td>Modifying or testing an idea under controlled conditions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Original Research</strong></td><td>Investigating a question beyond simply following a paper.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">
      A small-scale experiment on a consumer GPU is never described as
      reproducing a frontier model — results like that are labeled
      "conceptual small-scale reproduction."
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>Learning philosophy</h2>
    <p class="prompt">learn → implement → experiment → analyze → document → share → repeat</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>Community</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Reproductions, corrections, and discussion are welcome. See
      <a href={`${links.github}/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>
      and
      <a href={`${links.github}/blob/master/COMMUNITY.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">COMMUNITY.md</a>
      on GitHub.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
